{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 124, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-output residual is most valuable when it is absent (exps 71,75,78 gave +15-20 on IN16)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing input-output edge gives large gains (exps 11,15,18) versus replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the identity shortcut with a conv removes the residual path and was negative in exps 12,16,19."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 also absent, removing edge 0 cuts input to nodes 1 and 2, causing 10-20 point drops (exps 25-27)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 is dead, the node2->output path carries all computation, so a conv there helps a lot (exps 8-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool on the only path into node 1 with a conv consistently helped (exps 84,87,90)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Skip already passes useful features to node 1, so swapping it for a 1x1 conv gains little (exps 82,86,89)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv loses more capacity than removing skip or pool (exp 21 vs 22,23)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading skip to a 3x3 conv on node1->output wa